id: holy-transformation
name: Holy Transformation
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCostPerTier: 2
attacking: false
requiresTarget: false
usageLimit: 1/encounter
# A God Maneuver: open where an effect grants it, only in God Ki, its 2(T) paid in Divine Ki Points (maneuvers.mjs
# whyNotGod, spendManeuverCost). "Enter a Transformation with the God Ki Aspect ... considered the Transformation
# Maneuver for any effects" - and there is no Transformation Maneuver yet: until Transformations are built, its card
# says what it does and the table enters the Transformation, with no Stress Test for entering it.
godManeuver: true
says: >
  As the Transformation Maneuver: enter a Transformation with the God Ki Aspect, with no Stress Test for entering it -
  later ones as usual.
source: Core Rule
description: >
  A God Maneuver: enter a Transformation with the God Ki Aspect, no Stress Test for entering it.
text: >
  Holy Transformation [1/Encounter]: Transform with divine ease.
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –DKP Cost: 2(T)
  –Effect: Enter a Transformation with the God Ki Aspect. You do not roll a Stress Test for entering the Transformation,
  but any subsequent Stress Tests are rolled as usual. This Maneuver is considered the Transformation Maneuver for any
  effects.
